A||||8||fropuff||Removal of the "black stuff"...||||1||
Z||000000||fropuff||06-15-2001||06:06 PM||||Hey.  I want to paint the "black stuff" on my fastback GT, and I'm wondering how it, or if it, comes off.  The black stuff I'm referring to is the black "trim" that is on the rear, around the engine grilles, etc.  The stuff that goes around the sail panels, etc.  I'm wondering if it can come out.  It'd make it a lot easier than masking, etc.  If you know what I'm talking about, can it come off?  Thanks a lot!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||cadaver||06-15-2001||06:38 PM||||Yes it comes off. There are a couple of bolts and a square key thing held in with a screw near the back.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||06-15-2001||11:44 PM||||Great!  I'll get to it tomorrow!  I'm going to take off the mirrors as well and paint em up.  Thanks a lot!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000003||danny boy||06-16-2001||03:28 AM|||| When taking them off,pry the top out first,then tilt in towards engine and pull out. Be careful not to tear your trunk seal in the process.||||reg||1
